A virus is a type of malware that can spread from one computer to another. Once a virus infects a computer, it can cause damage to the computer's files or spread to other computers on the network.

To learn about viruses and how to protect against them, you can create a benign program that mimics virus behavior. A benign program is a program that does not cause any harm.

First, you will need to decide on the behavior of your benign program. For this tutorial, you can create a program that displays a message box when it is run.

To create the program, follow these steps:

1. Open Visual Studio and create a new project.
2. Replace the code in the Main method with the following code:

```csharp
MessageBox.Show("Hello, world!");
```
3. Save and run the program. You will see a message box display when you run the program.

```csharp
using System;

namespace BenignProgram
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            MessageBox.Show("Hello, world!");
        }
